#. type: Title =
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/build/commands.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build and run commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/build/commands.adoc
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/deployment/docker.adoc
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"__As of: 2026-11-06 · OpenEMS version 2026.12.0-SNAPSHOT (development "
"version, branch develop)__"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/build/commands.adoc
msgid ""
"This page is a quick reference for the commands. It complements the "
"xref:development/overview.adoc[Developer Guide overview], xref:edge/"
"build.adoc[Build OpenEMS Edge] and xref:ui/build.adoc[Build OpenEMS UI]. If "
"you do not yet know OSGi, bnd and Gradle, start with xref:development/"
"fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc[OSGi and tools]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/build/commands.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Repository structure"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/build/commands.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Path\n"
"| Content\n"
"\n"
"| `+io.openems.edge.*+`\n"
"| bundles of the Edge (devices, Controllers, core)\n"
"| `+io.openems.backend.*+`\n"
"| bundles of the Backend\n"
"| `+io.openems.common*+`, `+io.openems.core.*+`, `+io.openems.shared.*+`\n"
"| shared code\n"
"| `+cnf/+`\n"
"| bnd workspace configuration: dependencies (`+build.bnd+`), Checkstyle (`+checkstyle.xml+`)\n"
"| `+io.openems.edge.application/EdgeApp.bndrun+`\n"
"| start description of the Edge: framework, bundles, runtime parameters\n"
"| `+ui/+`\n"
"| Angular/Ionic UI\n"
"| `+doc/+`\n"
"| this documentation (Antora/AsciiDoc)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/build/commands.adoc
msgid ""
"Each bundle has the same structure: `+bnd.bnd+` (name, `+-buildpath+`, `+-"
"testpath+`), `+src/+`, `+test/+` and `+readme.adoc+`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/build/commands.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Building Edge and Backend"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-building-edge-and-backend
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/build/commands.adoc
msgid "All commands in the root directory of the repository:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/build/commands.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"./gradlew buildEdge          # Fat-JAR of the Edge to build/openems-edge.jar\n"
"./gradlew buildBackend       # Fat-JAR of the Backend to build/openems-backend.jar\n"
"./gradlew buildBackendEdge   # Fat-JAR of the Backend-Edge to build/openems-backend-edge.jar\n"
"./gradlew buildComponents    # compile all bundles without packing a JAR\n"
"./gradlew :io.openems.edge.meter.janitza:jar             # JAR of a single bundle to <bundle>/generated/\n"
"./gradlew :io.openems.edge.meter.janitza:test            # tests of a bundle\n"
"./gradlew :io.openems.edge.meter.janitza:checkstyleMain  # Checkstyle of a bundle\n"
"./gradlew checkstyleAll      # Checkstyle across all bundles\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/build/commands.adoc
msgid ""
"The target path of the JARs can be changed via the Gradle property "
"`+oems.edge.output+` or the environment variable `+OEMS_EDGE_OUTPUT+` (`+…"
"backend…+` accordingly)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/build/commands.adoc
msgid ""
"Checkstyle runs with zero warnings allowed. Before a pull request, "
"`+checkstyleMain+` should be free of errors for every changed bundle; see "
"also the xref:development/coding-guidelines.adoc[Coding Guidelines]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/build/commands.adoc
msgid ""
"A new bundle does not need to be entered in a list; Gradle finds all "
"directories with `+bnd.bnd+`. To be part of the Edge JAR, however, it must "
"be listed in `+EdgeApp.bndrun+` under `+-runrequires+`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/build/commands.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Starting the Edge locally"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/build/commands.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "java -jar build/openems-edge.jar\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/build/commands.adoc
msgid ""
"Without configuration, the Edge reports “There are no Schedulers "
"configured!” every second. This is normal."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/build/commands.adoc
msgid ""
"**Where the configuration is located:** `+EdgeApp.bndrun+` sets `+c:/openems/"
"config+` for the directory `+felix.cm.dir+` and `+openems.data.dir=c:/"
"openems/data+` for data (e.g. rrd4j history). On macOS or Linux these are "
"relative paths; a folder named `+c:+` is then created in the working "
"directory. You can set your own paths at startup:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/build/commands.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"java -Dfelix.cm.dir=$HOME/openems/config \\\n"
"     -Dopenems.data.dir=$HOME/openems/data \\\n"
"     -jar build/openems-edge.jar\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/build/commands.adoc
msgid ""
"**First configuration:** see xref:gettingstarted.adoc[Getting Started]. The "
"Apache Felix Web Console runs at `+http://localhost:8080/system/console/"
"configMgr+` (port from `+org.osgi.service.http.port+`). For experiments "
"without hardware, there are simulator bundles "
"(`+io.openems.edge.simulator+`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/build/commands.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "UI in development mode"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-building-the-ui
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/build/commands.adoc
msgid "In the directory `+ui/+`:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/build/commands.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"npm ci\n"
"npx ng serve -c openems-edge-dev       # connects to ws://<host>:8085 (Edge directly)\n"
"npx ng serve -c openems-backend-dev    # connects to the local Backend\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/build/commands.adoc
msgid ""
"The target URLs are in `+ui/src/themes/openems/environments/edge-dev.ts+` "
"and `+backend-dev.ts+`. Tests and lint:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/build/commands.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"npm test -- --watch=false --browsers=ChromeHeadlessCI\n"
"npm run lint\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/build/commands.adoc
msgid ""
"Changed texts in the UI must be added in `+ui/src/app/shared/i18n/+`; `+npm "
"run lint+` checks the translation keys."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/build/commands.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Building the UI"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/build/commands.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"npm ci\n"
"npx ng build -c \"openems,openems-edge-prod,prod\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/build/commands.adoc
msgid ""
"The result is in `+ui/target/+`: static files for a web server. The "
"configurations in `+ui/angular.json+` are combined:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/build/commands.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Configuration\n"
"| Effect\n"
"\n"
"| `+openems+`\n"
"| theme from `+src/themes/openems/+`\n"
"| `+prod+`\n"
"| production build: AOT, minified, file names with hash, without source maps, with license file\n"
"| `+openems-edge-prod+`\n"
"| Edge directly via `+ws(s)://<host>:8075+`. The default port of `+Controller.Api.Websocket+` is 8085, so change it there.\n"
"| `+openems-edge-docker+`\n"
"| Edge via `+ws(s)://<host>/openems-edge+`; needs the nginx proxy of the UI image\n"
"| `+openems-backend-prod+`\n"
"| Backend via `+ws(s)://<host>:8082+`\n"
"| `+openems-backend-docker+`\n"
"| Backend via `+ws(s)://<host>/openems-backend+`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/build/commands.adoc
msgid ""
"The addresses are in `+ui/src/themes/openems/environments/*.ts+`. A build "
"with `+-c \"openems,openems-edge-dev,prod\"+` is optimized and connects to "
"port 8085. New apps in the App Center do not require a UI build (see "
"xref:development/implementing/apps.adoc[Apps for the App Center])."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/build/commands.adoc
msgid ""
"As a Docker image, from the root directory of the repository (default "
"configuration `+openems,openems-edge-docker,prod+`, see xref:ui/deploy/"
"docker.adoc[Deploy UI to Docker]):"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/build/commands.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "docker build -f tools/docker/ui/Dockerfile.edge -t openems_ui_edge:custom .\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/build/commands.adoc
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/data/export.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Notes"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-notes
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/build/commands.adoc
msgid ""
"The Edge targets weak hardware (about 1 GB RAM, 2 cores). Computationally "
"intensive logic does not belong in every Cycle."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-notes
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/build/commands.adoc
msgid ""
"The repository contains `+CLAUDE.md+` and `+AGENTS.md+` with short rules for "
"code style and tests."
msgstr ""
